                                                "example_id": "ad3ee71a-0264-48df-8070-7cded98d002a",
                                                "sense_id": "4539a3e1-19ef-35c4-acbf-45dc04356819",
                                                "text": "The Outer city, also known as the Chinese city, was added during the reign of the emperor Chia Ching (1522-66) of the Ming dynasty. It is in the form of an oblong adjoining the Inner city. with walls 14 mi. in length, including 4 mi. of the southern wall of the Inner city."
